      "writtenOn": "2019-04-19T07:22:24Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Is this really what we agreed on ? I remember something closer to :\n\nThe device SHOULD support keepalive offload. If it does not, it MUST reply with {@link SocketKeepalive.Callback#onError} with {@code ERROR_UNSUPPORTED} to any keepalive offload request. If it does, it MUST support at least 3 concurrent keepalive slots.\n\nThe issue I have with your wording of 3 concurrent slots per network is that if you have 3 networks then you need 30 slots. Even if that\u0027s true then I still think we should make clear that if it\u0027s supported then it must support at least 3 per network.",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 47,
        "startChar": 3,
        "endLine": 48,
        "endChar": 71
      },
      "revId": "67b53fcc0630d6d7d45292a328f5a36781acaf52",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889",
      "unresolved": true
    },
    {
      "key": {
        "uuid": "f239f19d_4351552c",
        "filename": "core/java/android/net/SocketKeepalive.java",
        "patchSetId": 5
